{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0da0efc0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "title: \"Module Isolation Dashboard — Controlled-Input Response Surfaces\"\n",
    "format: html\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## What This Code Does\n",
    "\n",
    "This demo exercises all 5 phases **in isolation** — each section varies only one module's inputs while holding all other state fixed. This proves each module's response surface is correct independent of the others.\n",
    "\n",
    "The theory predicts: stress perception monotonicity (omega_c → challenge, omega_o → hindrance), resilience activation copes-successfully when challenge > hindrance, resource allocation concentrates on high-efficacy PF with low temperature, stress buffering mediates stress through resources (a × b ≠ 0), and daily cycle resets affect toward baseline.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Setup"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "setup",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#| label: setup\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "import pathlib\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from numpy.random import Generator, PCG64\n",
    "\n",
    "demos_dir = pathlib.Path(os.getcwd())\n",
    "project_root = demos_dir.parents[2]\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, str(project_root))\n",
    "\n",
    "from src.python.phases.stress_perception import run_phase as run_perception\n",
    "from src.python.phases.resilience_activation import run_phase as run_activation\n",
    "from src.python.phases.resource_allocation import run_phase as run_allocation\n",
    "from src.python.phases.stress_buffering import run_phase as run_buffering\n",
    "from src.python.phases.interfaces import AgentState, PhaseOutput\n",
    "from src.python.demos.module_metrics import compute_isolation_inputs\n",
    "\n",
    "_FACTORS = [\"social_support\", \"family_support\", \"formal_intervention\", \"psychological_capital\"]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ccb1be73",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Module 1 — Stress Perception: Omega_c × Omega_o Sweep\n",
    "\n",
    "Challenge rises with omega_c; hindrance rises with omega_o. The effective threshold = base + 0.15×challenge − 0.25×hindrance."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "module-perception",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Perception: 400 points\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#| label: module-perception\n",
    "rng = Generator(PCG64(42))\n",
    "records = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for omega_c in np.linspace(0, 1, 20):\n",
    "    for omega_o in np.linspace(0, 1, 20):\n",
    "        state = AgentState(\n",
    "            stress_controllability=0.5, stress_overload=0.5,\n",
    "            volatility=0.5, recent_stress_intensity=0.0,\n",
    "            stress_momentum=0.0, resilience=0.5,\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        config = {\"omega_c\": omega_c, \"omega_o\": omega_o, \"bias\": 0.0,\n",
    "                  \"gamma\": 6.0, \"delta\": 0.2, \"base_threshold\": 0.5,\n",
    "                  \"challenge_scale\": 0.15, \"hindrance_scale\": 0.25}\n",
    "        out = run_perception(state, config, rng)\n",
    "        records.append({\n",
    "            \"omega_c\": omega_c, \"omega_o\": omega_o,\n",
    "            \"challenge\": out[\"observation\"][\"challenge\"],\n",
    "            \"hindrance\": out[\"observation\"][\"hindrance\"],\n",
    "            \"appraised_stress\": out[\"observation\"][\"appraised_stress\"],\n",
    "            \"effective_threshold\": out[\"observation\"][\"effective_threshold\"],\n",
    "            \"is_stressed\": int(out[\"observation\"][\"is_stressed\"]),\n",
    "        })\n",
    "\n",
    "df_perception = pd.DataFrame(records)\n",
    "print(f\"Perception: {len(df_perception)} points\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1bfb3f58",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Module 2 — Resilience Activation: Challenge × Hindrance × Neighbor Affect\n",
    "\n",
    "Coping probability rises with challenge/hindrance ratio. Positive neighbors improve odds."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "module-activation",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Activation: 1200 points\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#| label: module-activation\n",
    "rng = Generator(PCG64(42))\n",
    "records = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for neighbor_affect in [-0.5, 0.0, 0.5]:\n",
    "    for challenge in np.linspace(0, 1, 20):\n",
    "        for hindrance in np.linspace(0, 1, 20):\n",
    "            state = AgentState(\n",
    "                affect=0.0, resilience=0.5, current_stress=0.3,\n",
    "                baseline_resilience=0.5, challenge=challenge, hindrance=hindrance,\n",
    "                protective_factors={f: 0.5 for f in _FACTORS},\n",
    "                resources=0.6, stress_controllability=0.5, stress_overload=0.5,\n",
    "                volatility=0.3, recent_stress_intensity=0.0, stress_momentum=0.0,\n",
    "            )\n",
    "            config = {\"neighbor_affects\": [neighbor_affect], \"base_resource_cost\": 0.1}\n",
    "            out = run_activation(state, config, rng)\n",
    "            records.append({\n",
    "                \"challenge\": challenge, \"hindrance\": hindrance,\n",
    "                \"neighbor_affect\": neighbor_affect,\n",
    "                \"coping_probability\": out[\"observation\"][\"coping_probability\"],\n",
    "                \"coped_successfully\": int(out[\"observation\"][\"coped_successfully\"]),\n",
    "                \"resilience_effect\": out[\"observation\"][\"resilience_effect\"],\n",
    "                \"delta_stress\": out[\"observation\"][\"delta_stress\"],\n",
    "                \"delta_affect\": out[\"observation\"][\"delta_affect\"],\n",
    "            })\n",
    "\n",
    "df_activation = pd.DataFrame(records)\n",
    "print(f\"Activation: {len(df_activation)} points\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5240ebf5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Module 3 — Resource Allocation: Resources × Softmax Temperature\n",
    "\n",
    "High temperature → uniform allocation. Low temperature → winner-take-most."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "module-allocation",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Allocation: 270 points\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#| label: module-allocation\n",
    "rng = Generator(PCG64(42))\n",
    "records = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for day in range(30):\n",
    "    for resources in [0.2, 0.5, 0.8]:\n",
    "        for temperature in [0.5, 1.0, 5.0]:\n",
    "            state = AgentState(\n",
    "                resources=resources, affect=0.0, resilience=0.5,\n",
    "                protective_factors={f: 0.5 for f in _FACTORS},\n",
    "            )\n",
    "            config = {\"base_regeneration\": 0.1, \"softmax_temperature\": temperature,\n",
    "                      \"protective_improvement_rate\": 0.1}\n",
    "            out = run_allocation(state, config, rng)\n",
    "            records.append({\n",
    "                \"day\": day, \"resources_start\": resources, \"temperature\": temperature,\n",
    "                \"regeneration_amount\": out[\"observation\"][\"regeneration_amount\"],\n",
    "                \"resources_after\": out[\"state_delta\"].get(\"resources\", resources),\n",
    "            })\n",
    "\n",
    "df_allocation = pd.DataFrame(records)\n",
    "print(f\"Allocation: {len(df_allocation)} points\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "147e160b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Module 4 — Stress Buffering: Current Stress Sweep (Baron & Kenny)\n",
    "\n",
    "Current stress depletes resources (a-path). Resources enhance buffering (b-path). Residual direct effect (c'-path)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "module-buffering",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Buffering: 30 points\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#| label: module-buffering\n",
    "rng = Generator(PCG64(42))\n",
    "records = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for current_stress in np.linspace(0, 1, 30):\n",
    "    state = AgentState(\n",
    "        current_stress=current_stress, resilience=0.5, baseline_resilience=0.5,\n",
    "        protective_factors={f: 0.5 for f in _FACTORS},\n",
    "        resources=0.5, stress_overload=0.5,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    config = {}\n",
    "    out = run_buffering(state, config, rng)\n",
    "    records.append({\n",
    "        \"current_stress\": current_stress,\n",
    "        \"resources_before\": 0.5,\n",
    "        \"resources_after\": out[\"state_delta\"].get(\"resources\", 0.5),\n",
    "        \"buffering_strength\": out[\"observation\"][\"buffering_strength\"],\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\n",
    "df_buffering = pd.DataFrame(records)\n",
    "print(f\"Buffering: {len(df_buffering)} points\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6c7754bf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Module 5 — Daily Cycle: Affect × Current Stress Reset\n",
    "\n",
    "Affect moves toward baseline. Stress decays. Reset magnitude = pre − post deviation from baseline."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "module-daily-cycle",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Daily cycle: 150 points\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#| label: module-daily-cycle\n",
    "from src.python.agent import process_daily_reset\n",
    "\n",
    "rng = Generator(PCG64(42))\n",
    "records = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for affect in np.linspace(-1, 1, 15):\n",
    "    for current_stress in np.linspace(0, 1, 10):\n",
    "        pre_state = AgentState(affect=affect, baseline_affect=0.0,\n",
    "                               current_stress=current_stress)\n",
    "        config = {\"current_day\": 0}\n",
    "        out = process_daily_reset(pre_state, config, rng)\n",
    "        post_affect = out[\"state_delta\"].get(\"affect\", affect)\n",
    "        post_stress = out[\"state_delta\"].get(\"current_stress\", current_stress)\n",
    "        reset_mag = abs(affect - 0.0) - abs(post_affect - 0.0)\n",
    "        records.append({\n",
    "            \"affect\": affect, \"current_stress\": current_stress,\n",
    "            \"post_affect\": post_affect, \"post_stress\": post_stress,\n",
    "            \"affect_reset_magnitude\": max(0.0, reset_mag),\n",
    "            \"stress_decay_amount\": max(0.0, current_stress - post_stress),\n",
    "        })\n",
    "\n",
    "df_daily = pd.DataFrame(records)\n",
    "print(f\"Daily cycle: {len(df_daily)} points\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b88b4124",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Response Surfaces Summary"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "summary",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1440x864 with 8 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {
      "image/png": {
       "height": 852,
       "width": 1430
      }
     },
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#| label: summary\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 3, figsize=(15, 9))\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Perception: challenge surface\n",
    "piv = df_perception.pivot_table(index=\"omega_c\", columns=\"omega_o\", values=\"challenge\")\n",
    "sns.heatmap(piv, ax=axes[0, 0], cmap=\"Blues\", cbar_kws={\"label\": \"challenge\"})\n",
    "axes[0, 0].set_title(\"Perception: Challenge(omega_c, omega_o)\")\n",
    "axes[0, 0].set_xlabel(\"omega_o\"); axes[0, 0].set_ylabel(\"omega_c\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Activation: coping prob surface (neighbor_affect=0)\n",
    "sub = df_activation[df_activation[\"neighbor_affect\"] == 0.0]\n",
    "piv = sub.pivot_table(index=\"challenge\", columns=\"hindrance\", values=\"coping_probability\")\n",
    "sns.heatmap(piv, ax=axes[0, 1], cmap=\"RdYlGn\", cbar_kws={\"label\": \"coping prob\"})\n",
    "axes[0, 1].set_title(\"Activation: Coping Probability\")\n",
    "axes[0, 1].set_xlabel(\"hindrance\"); axes[0, 1].set_ylabel(\"challenge\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# 3. Allocation: resources over time\n",
    "sub = df_allocation[df_allocation[\"temperature\"] == 1.0]\n",
    "sns.lineplot(data=sub, x=\"day\", y=\"resources_after\", hue=\"resources_start\",\n",
    "             ax=axes[0, 2], palette=\"Set2\")\n",
    "axes[0, 2].set_title(\"Allocation: Resources Trajectory\")\n",
    "axes[0, 2].set_ylabel(\"resources after\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# 4. Buffering: stress vs buffering\n",
    "sns.scatterplot(data=df_buffering, x=\"current_stress\", y=\"buffering_strength\",\n",
    "                ax=axes[1, 0], alpha=0.7)\n",
    "axes[1, 0].set_title(\"Buffering: Stress vs Buffering Strength\")\n",
    "axes[1, 0].set_xlabel(\"current_stress\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# 5. Daily cycle: affect reset\n",
    "sns.scatterplot(data=df_daily, x=\"affect\", y=\"affect_reset_magnitude\",\n",
    "                hue=\"current_stress\", ax=axes[1, 1], alpha=0.6, palette=\"viridis\")\n",
    "axes[1, 1].set_title(\"Daily Cycle: Affect Reset\")\n",
    "axes[1, 1].axhline(0, color=\"grey\", linestyle=\"--\", alpha=0.5)\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[1, 2].axis(\"off\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6b00aad3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## What We See\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Perception**: challenge monotonic in omega_c; hindrance monotonic in omega_o; threshold complementarity\n",
    "- **Activation**: coping probability rises with challenge/hindrance ratio; positive neighbors shift curve up\n",
    "- **Allocation**: low temperature concentrates resources; high temperature distributes uniformly\n",
    "- **Buffering**: stress depletes resources (negative a-path); buffering strength tracks remaining resources\n",
    "- **Daily cycle**: affect pulled toward baseline; stress decays; reset magnitude proportional to deviation\n",
    "\n",
    "## Why This Matters\n",
    "\n",
    "Isolation mode proves each module's response surface is correct before composing them in the full simulation. The dashboard view lets you compare all 5 modules side by side."
   ]
  }
 ],
